  "term": "inner hair cells",
  "definition": "Inner hair cells are the sound-sensing cells in the organ of Corti of the inner ear. They are typically arranged in a single row toward the modiolus, are fewer than outer hair cells, and have stereocilia that are about twice as thick.",
